From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:31:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: put pitch-layout offscreen GEM memory in system
 memory

GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR buffers without SCANOUT, which both NVIDIA's GBM
backend and ours allocate as pitch layout with NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT,
are what userspace allocates to share with other devices: an iGPU that
renders or displays them, or a USB or BMC display. Those importers need
the buffer's pages, but nvidia-drm can't give a scatterlist for video
memory (prime_get_sg_table returns -ENOMEM), so the import fails and the
buffer can't leave the NVIDIA GPU.

Allocate such memory in system memory from the start; its pages work for
every importer. NVIDIA's GL can't render to pitch-linear images, so
same-GPU use of these buffers is limited to sampling and uploads.
Block-linear and scanout memory stays in video memory, and the
video-to-system-memory fallback only runs when video memory was tried.

Refusing the attachment instead would break importers like udl and gud
that only vmap the buffer, which works for video memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c      | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
index a2d71782..760fbba4 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
@@ -718,7 +718,17 @@ int nv_drm_gem_alloc_nvkms_memory_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
     allocParams.type = (p->flags & NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT) ?
         NVKMS_KAPI_ALLOCATION_TYPE_OFFSCREEN : NVKMS_KAPI_ALLOCATION_TYPE_SCANOUT;
     allocParams.size = p->memory_size;
-    allocParams.useVideoMemory = nv_dev->hasVideoMemory;
+    /*
+     * Pitch-layout offscreen memory (GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR without SCANOUT) is
+     * what userspace allocates to share with other devices: an iGPU
+     * rendering or displaying it, a USB or BMC display. Importers need its
+     * pages (prime_get_sg_table), which video memory doesn't have, so put
+     * it in system memory from the start. NVIDIA's GL can't render to
+     * pitch-linear images anyway, so same-GPU use is limited to sampling
+     * and uploads. Block-linear and scanout memory stays in video memory.
+     */
+    allocParams.useVideoMemory = nv_dev->hasVideoMemory &&
+        (p->block_linear || !(p->flags & NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT));
     allocParams.compressible = &p->compressible;
 
     pMemory = nvKms->allocateMemory(nv_dev->pDevice, &allocParams);
@@ -740,7 +750,8 @@ int nv_drm_gem_alloc_nvkms_memory_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
         pMemory = nvKms->allocateMemory(nv_dev->pDevice, &allocParams);
     }
 
-    if (pMemory == NULL && (p->flags & NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT)) {
+    if (pMemory == NULL && allocParams.useVideoMemory &&
+        (p->flags & NV_GEM_ALLOC_NO_SCANOUT)) {
         if (__ratelimit(&log_rs)) {
             NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_INFO(
                     nv_dev,
